{
    "word": "sardonyx",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "de60f48b-a56a-3f75-9262-ff5c0b75c993",
                "word": "sardonyx",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d5a96772-16b0-442a-b04a-c7a19329d237",
                        "entry_id": "de60f48b-a56a-3f75-9262-ff5c0b75c993",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sardonyxes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18f1b1b5-1a0e-33b1-9d5e-9b3bee3dfabd",
                        "entry_id": "de60f48b-a56a-3f75-9262-ff5c0b75c993",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A gemstone having bands of red sard; a variety of onyx or chalcedony."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff55c3ed-d00b-415f-8ced-789c897085ec",
                                "sense_id": "18f1b1b5-1a0e-33b1-9d5e-9b3bee3dfabd",
                                "text": "The fifth, sardonyx; the sixth, sardius; the seventh, chrysolyte; the eighth, beryl; the ninth, a topaz; the tenth, a chrysoprasus; the eleventh, a jacinth; the twelfth, an amethyst."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca1c8d13-c7c4-4df8-b3b6-e3d913dccc73",
                                "sense_id": "18f1b1b5-1a0e-33b1-9d5e-9b3bee3dfabd",
                                "text": "The large chalice at right is carved from a single chunk of sardonyx, a kind of onyx. Its gilded rim and base are decorated with tiny enamels depicting a host of popular saints, including Nicephorus (farthest left on rim), a Ninth Century patriarch and opponent of a religious movement to destroy icons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e50f6468-0925-4e03-8d4b-d01f9065156d",
                                "sense_id": "18f1b1b5-1a0e-33b1-9d5e-9b3bee3dfabd",
                                "text": "I was wondering at these hanging gardens amid the forest of pink and white marble, red sardonyx, blue-gray, and cream, and black bricks, and green and yellow and tyrian tiles, when the sight of a lansquenet guarding the entrance to a casern reminded me of the promise I had made the officer of the peltasts the night before."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7a1d533a-c9f7-4f90-9340-2d610c4eb42d",
                        "source_entry_id": "de60f48b-a56a-3f75-9262-ff5c0b75c993",
                        "source_sense_id": "18f1b1b5-1a0e-33b1-9d5e-9b3bee3dfabd",
                        "source_sense_description": "gemstone banded with red sard",
                        "target_lang_word": "sardoine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sardoine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c86ded1-d4de-3328-b43d-3581f5832c4a",
                                        "entry_id": "79069fef-f659-3759-8b79-bc2c49c99c58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte d’agate, d’une couleur brune, avec des reflets orangés."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e475354-d778-4d08-8ba1-b360e58cd94c",
                                                "sense_id": "2c86ded1-d4de-3328-b43d-3581f5832c4a",
                                                "text": "Anne lui apparut plus belle que de coutume, belle de la beauté de ces sardoines afghanes qui, parvenues à la moitié de leur carrière, se mettent à flamber tout à coup d’une flamme éclatante et triste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ffe2793-fbc0-484a-97c5-c78b1efed70e",
                                                "sense_id": "2c86ded1-d4de-3328-b43d-3581f5832c4a",
                                                "text": "Elle montait parfois les deux marches qui menaient aux profondes embrasures des fenêtres pour exposer aux derniers rayons du soleil la transparence des sardoines, et, tout enveloppée de l'or oblique du crépuscule, Valentine elle-même semblait diaphane comme ses gemmes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ba7c5d8-8e35-479f-a1d8-78a24e39adc3",
                                                "sense_id": "2c86ded1-d4de-3328-b43d-3581f5832c4a",
                                                "text": "émeraudes, jaspe, rubis, sardoines, escarboucles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de740087-401e-41c6-8fc6-aacc53043aa0",
                                                "sense_id": "2c86ded1-d4de-3328-b43d-3581f5832c4a",
                                                "text": "Nous avons acquis un précieux calice fait d’une seule sardoine massive, ainsi qu’un autre vase de même matière, mais non de même forme, ressemblant à une amphore, et encore un autre vase qui semble comme de béryl ou de cristal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b17525c9-e207-4b57-89d5-08c05af1802b",
                        "source_entry_id": "de60f48b-a56a-3f75-9262-ff5c0b75c993",
